---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Security patches — LemmaScript Solutions"
  description="Close security vulnerabilities not just for the known proof-of-concept but for every input — a contract on the fixed function that holds across all cases."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">// solutions / security patches</span>
      <h1>A fix that holds for <em>every input.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A patch that closes the known proof-of-concept still leaves every input
        nobody thought of unguarded. LemmaScript closes that gap: the contract
        defines what the fixed function must hold across all inputs — not just the
        one in the advisory.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- CONTRACT IN ACTION -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="kicker">// contract in action</span>
        <h2>The fix applied in place — guaranteed for every encoding.</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          CVE-2026-39410: a non-breaking space (<code class="t-anno">0xA0</code>) let a malformed cookie name
          masquerade as valid. The contract locks the exact set of characters
          that may ever be stripped — for every input, not just the known bypass.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="codeblock">
        <div class="code-bar">
          <span class="code-file">src/utils/cookie.ts</span>
          <a href="https://github.com/midspiral/hono-lemmascript/blob/lemmascript/src/utils/cookie.ts#L79" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="code-gh-link">View on GitHub ↗</a>
        </div>
        <pre class="code-body"><span class="t-kw">const</span> <span class="t-fn">trimCookieWhitespace</span> = (value: string): string =&gt; &#123;
  <span class="t-anno">//@ ensures \result.length &lt;= value.length</span>
  <span class="t-cmt">// CVE-2026-39410: only space (0x20) and tab (0x09) are stripped — nothing else (e.g. 0xA0).</span>
  <span class="t-anno">//@ ensures \result.length &gt; 0 ==&gt;</span>
  <span class="t-anno">//@   \result.charCodeAt(0) !== 0x20 &amp;&amp; \result.charCodeAt(0) !== 0x09</span>

  <span class="t-kw">let</span> start = 0
  <span class="t-kw">let</span> end = value.length
  <span class="t-kw">while</span> (start &lt; end) &#123;
    <span class="t-kw">const</span> charCode = value.charCodeAt(start)
    <span class="t-kw">if</span> (charCode !== <span class="t-num">0x20</span> &amp;&amp; charCode !== <span class="t-num">0x09</span>) <span class="t-kw">break</span>
    start++
  &#125;
  <span class="t-cmt">// …end trimmed by the same rule…</span>
  <span class="t-kw">return</span> value.slice(start, end)
&#125;</pre>
      </div>
      <p class="code-caption">
        From <a href="https://github.com/midspiral/hono-lemmascript" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-arrow">hono-lemmascript ↗</a> — the production cookie parser, contract applied in place.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BYPASS DIAGRAM -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="kicker">// what changes</span>
        <h2>From "known exploit blocked" to "entire class blocked."</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          A patch closes the specific input in the advisory. A contract closes every input
          in the same family — the ones in the advisory, and every variant nobody listed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bypass-diagram">
        <div class="bypass-col">
          <span class="bypass-title">Patched — no contract</span>
          <div class="bypass-inputs">
            <div class="bypass-input bypass-blocked">
              <span class="bypass-val"><code>\xA0sessionId</code></span>
              <span class="bypass-verdict verdict-blocked">blocked</span>
              <span class="bypass-note">the known POC</span>
            </div>
            <div class="bypass-input bypass-unknown">
              <span class="bypass-val"><code> sessionId</code></span>
              <span class="bypass-verdict verdict-unknown">?</span>
              <span class="bypass-note">em space — uncharted</span>
            </div>
            <div class="bypass-input bypass-unknown">
              <span class="bypass-val"><code>­sessionId</code></span>
              <span class="bypass-verdict verdict-unknown">?</span>
              <span class="bypass-note">soft hyphen — uncharted</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bypass-vs">→</div>

        <div class="bypass-col">
          <span class="bypass-title bypass-title-good">Contract in place</span>
          <div class="bypass-inputs">
            <div class="bypass-input bypass-blocked-good">
              <span class="bypass-val"><code>\xA0sessionId</code></span>
              <span class="bypass-verdict verdict-good">blocked</span>
              <span class="bypass-note">the known POC</span>
            </div>
            <div class="bypass-input bypass-blocked-good">
              <span class="bypass-val"><code> sessionId</code></span>
              <span class="bypass-verdict verdict-good">blocked</span>
              <span class="bypass-note">guaranteed by contract</span>
            </div>
            <div class="bypass-input bypass-blocked-good">
              <span class="bypass-val"><code>­sessionId</code></span>
              <span class="bypass-verdict verdict-good">blocked</span>
              <span class="bypass-note">guaranteed by contract</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="diagram-note">The contract says what may ever be stripped — so everything else is guaranteed safe.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT YOU GET -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="kicker">// what you get</span>
        <h2>A vulnerability that can't come back.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="what-grid">
        <div class="what-item">
          <h3>Every input in the class</h3>
          <p>The contract covers all inputs — alternate encodings, edge cases, forms the advisory never mentioned. If it can exploit the bug, the contract blocks it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="what-item">
          <h3>Applied in place</h3>
          <p>The guarantee lives in the production function, not a separate test. No copy to drift out of sync, no guard to accidentally remove.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="what-item">
          <h3>Regression-proof</h3>
          <p>Refactor the function and the contract re-checks from scratch. If the vulnerability class reappears, it fails the check before it ships.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- EXAMPLE -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="kicker">// example</span>
        <h2>Four CVEs in a production web framework — guaranteed closed.</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          A fork of the Hono web framework with four real CVEs guaranteed closed —
          IP restriction bypass, cookie-name bypass, and two directory-traversal
          variants — applied directly to existing, production-grade middleware.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ex-stats">
        <div class="ex-stat">
          <span class="ex-val">4</span>
          <span class="ex-label">real CVEs guaranteed closed</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ex-stat">
          <span class="ex-val">6/6</span>
          <span class="ex-label">existing middleware tests still pass</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ex-stat">
          <span class="ex-val">in-place</span>
          <span class="ex-label">function behavior left unchanged</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ex-actions">
        <a href="/case-studies/hono" class="btn btn-primary">Read the case study →</a>
        <a href="/solutions" class="btn btn-secondary">All solutions</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .code-gh-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-caption);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-left: auto;
  }
  .code-gh-link:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .code-caption {
    font-size: var(--fs-caption);
    color: var(--text-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    margin-top: var(--sp-4);
  }

  /* bypass diagram */
  .bypass-diagram {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--sp-8);
    padding: var(--sp-8) 0;
  }
  .bypass-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-4);
    flex: 1;
    max-width: 340px;
  }
  .bypass-title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-small);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .bypass-title-good { color: var(--accent); }
  .bypass-inputs { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--sp-3); }
  .bypass-input {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    grid-template-rows: auto auto;
    gap: var(--sp-1) var(--sp-3);
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--sp-4);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
  }
  .bypass-blocked { border-color: rgba(244,85,78,0.2); background: var(--state-counter-bg); }
  .bypass-unknown { border-color: rgba(245,196,81,0.2); background: var(--state-pending-bg); }
  .bypass-blocked-good { border-color: var(--accent-dim); background: var(--state-verified-bg); }

  .bypass-val { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--fs-caption); color: var(--text-secondary); grid-row: 1; grid-column: 1; }
  .bypass-val code { font-family: inherit; }
  .bypass-note { font-size: var(--fs-caption); color: var(--text-muted); grid-row: 2; grid-column: 1; }
  .bypass-verdict { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--fs-caption); font-weight: 700; grid-row: 1 / 3; grid-column: 2; white-space: nowrap; }
  .verdict-blocked { color: var(--state-counter); }
  .verdict-unknown { color: var(--state-pending); }
  .verdict-good { color: var(--accent); }

  .bypass-vs {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    align-self: center;
    padding-top: var(--sp-10);
  }

  .diagram-note {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--fs-small);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    margin-top: var(--sp-4);
  }

  /* shared */
  .what-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--sp-4); }
  .what-item { background: var(--bg-surface); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--r-lg); padding: var(--sp-6); }
  .what-item h3 { font-size: var(--fs-h3); margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); }
  .what-item p { font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; }

  .ex-stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--sp-4); margin-bottom: var(--sp-10); }
  .ex-stat { background: var(--bg-surface); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--r-lg); padding: var(--sp-6); }
  .ex-val { display: block; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: var(--sp-2); }
  .ex-label { font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--text-muted); }
  .ex-actions { display: flex; gap: var(--sp-3); flex-wrap: wrap; }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .bypass-diagram { flex-direction: column; align-items: center; }
    .bypass-vs { padding-top: 0; }
    .bypass-col { max-width: 100%; width: 100%; }
    .what-grid, .ex-stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
